{:id "0033-lab-crawl-camera"
 :title "Lab: the camera becomes data, and old lines recede into the distance"
 :lupa/deps #{"0032-lab-steady-line"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "Two things Ben's second recording showed. Long drafts run off the
        top of the stage (the first line cut, the floor gone), because
        nothing handles text taller than the screen. And the camera is
        decided inside the renderer, so no shot can ever be tested. Make
        the camera part of every frame (pure, in em units), keep the line
        being written in front of it, and let finished lines recede up and
        back into the dark, like an end-credits crawl, so the draft uses
        depth instead of falling off the screen."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/pose_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/render.cljs" "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs"
         "public/lab/index.html" "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"]
 :design "Schema (already in halfahead.schema, do not edit): :ha/camera
          {:x :y :z :tx :ty :tz :fov}, optional :camera on :ha/glyph-frame.
          pose/frame: opts gain :aspect (viewport width / height, from
          main.cljs). The frame always carries :camera:
          - Target (tx ty tz): x at the column's centre (width-em / 2), y at
            the line being written (the line of the last live glyph, or line
            0), z 0. When the current line changes, the target eases from
            the previous line's y to the new one over 450 ms, timed from the
            born-ms of the first glyph on the new line. Pure: a function of
            the draft and t, no stored state.
          - Position: in front of the target, pitched down at most 8
            degrees, at the distance where the column width fills about 75%
            of the view horizontally for the given :aspect and :fov (40).
          Crawl, in poses: lines more than 3 lines above the current line
          recede, each further line a step more: z moves back 0.9 em per
          line beyond 3, opacity scales down 0.18 per line (never below
          0.12), and the line tilts back (rx up to -0.5 rad). The recession
          is part of the line's base, so it holds when settled and
          everything still settles exactly onto it. The current line and
          the 3 above it are untouched.
          render.cljs follows :camera from the frame and decides nothing
          about where to look; remove its own following and easing. Keep
          window.__lab.lean and block-centre working (now against the
          frame's camera). Widen the debug overlay box so its first line is
          never clipped (it was cut at 'worst 18.0 r' on Ben's screen) and
          add the camera target to it.
          e2e/lab.mjs: keep every step; add one that types 14 lines of text
          and asserts every live glyph is either projected inside the
          viewport or has opacity <= 0.3, that the current line is inside
          the middle 60% of the viewport height, and screenshots
          out/lab/crawl.png."
 :acceptance
 ["Property: every frame now has a valid :camera; the camera is a pure
   function of (draft, t, opts) (equal inputs, equal camera)"
  "Property: the settling property still holds, with recession included in
   the settled base (lines more than 3 above the current one settle at
   their receded z, opacity and rx)"
  "Property: live chars still spell the draft; reduced motion still leaves
   live poses at their (receded) bases and the camera on its target with no
   easing"
  "Test: after the current line changes, the camera target y is between the
   old and new line's y at +225 ms and equal to the new line's y at +450 ms"
  "`bb lab:e2e` passes with the crawl step and the existing lean, steady
   and centring steps; the final message lists the screenshots"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["No shots, styles or director yet (later orders); no schema edits"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/schema.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/render.cljs" "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs"
           "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 12.0}
